From e9d3a222996782085787d0fca4dea492ecb8c57f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98ystein=20Lie?= <oeystein@gengartv.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:50:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] media: gc550: add USB command bridge and hardware
 initialization
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add USB command bridge protocol and peripheral initialization
sequence for the AVerMedia Live Gamer Extreme (GC550).

The command protocol communicates via Bulk OUT 0x01 and Bulk IN 0x81
to encapsulate I2C transactions to on-board peripherals (ADV7604,
ADV7511, PCA9539A GPIO expander, TLV320AIC3x codec, and Lattice FPGA).

Key functionality:
- gc550_cmd_send/xfer handling synchronous USB bulk messages.
- gc550_i2c_write/read helper functions.
- gc550_detect_board_state for warm-restart detection.
- Active hardware protection filter blocking Atmel AT88SC CryptoMemory
  opcodes (0x05, 0x06, 0x07, 0x09) to prevent security lockout.
- 53,146-byte peripheral initialization sequence (gc550_init_blob).

NOTE: The 53,146-byte initialization array is marked as BLOCKED
pending formal upstream provenance and licensing clarification
regarding its reverse-engineered origin.

Signed-off-by: Øystein Lie <oeystein@gengartv.com>
